<title>UK: EU seen awarding up to 60,000 T sugar at tender.</title>
<headline>EU seen awarding up to 60,000 T sugar at tender.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union (EU) is expected to award up to 60,000 tonnes of current series white sugar at its weekly tender later on Wednesday, traders said.</p>
<p>Last week the EU awarded 54,500 tonnes at a maximum rebate of 44.329 Ecus.</p>
<p>This week's maximum restitution level was estimated at 43.737 Ecus (European currency units) per 100 kilos of sugar based on the second-month August contract in Paris.</p>
<p>Licences are currently valid until the end of September.</p>
<p>--Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
